{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And you shall make it.</b> That each of the spices absorb one from the other, so that from all of them a single compound is made." "<b>The work of a perfumer.</b> That each of the spices be pounded as is appropriate for it, for a single manner of pounding does not suit each of the spices alike." "<b>Salted.</b> That the spices be thoroughly mixed, so that none of them is separated." "<b>Pure.</b> Clean of all impurity. This was necessary because the burning was done with the spice itself, but for the anointing oil this was not necessary because the bodies of the spices were not mixed into the oil at all."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:36.920374842Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}